  "answer_text": "Hipparchus (c. 190\u2013120 BC) was an ancient Greek astronomer and mathematician who is often called the \"father of astronomy.\" Here are his major inventions and contributions:\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udcd0 1. **Trigonometry**\nHe made an early contribution to trigonometry by producing a table of chords, an early example of a trigonometric table; indeed, some historians go so far as to say that trigonometry was invented by him. The purpose of this table of chords was to give a method for solving triangles which avoided solving each triangle from first principles.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf0d 2. **Precession of the Equinoxes**\nHipparchus discovered the precession of equinoxes by comparing his notes with earlier observers; his realization that the points of solstice and equinox moved slowly from east to west against the fixed background of the stars was one of his most significant achievements.\n\n---\n\n### \u2b50 3. **First Star Catalog**\nHe is credited with creating the first reliable star catalog, which included approximately 850 stars and established a system of stellar magnitude.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd2d 4. **Astronomical Instruments (including the Astrolabe)**\nHipparchus is credited with the invention or improvement of several astronomical instruments. According to Synesius of Ptolemais (4th century), he made the first astrolabion: this may have been an armillary sphere or the predecessor of the planar instrument called the astrolabe.\n\n---\n\n### \u2600\ufe0f\ud83c\udf19 5. **Models for the Sun and Moon**\nHe was the first Greek to develop quantitative and accurate models for the motion of the Sun and Moon, making use of the observations and knowledge accumulated over centuries by the Chaldeans from Babylonia.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf11 6. **Predicting Solar Eclipses**\nBased on his solar and lunar theories and his numerical trigonometry, he was probably the first to develop a reliable method to predict solar eclipses.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udcc5 7. **Calculating the Length of the Year**\nHipparchus calculated the length of the year to within 6.5 minutes and discovered the precession of the equinoxes.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f 8. **Latitude and Longitude**\nHe developed tools for measuring celestial angles and contributed to the systematic use of geographic coordinates, pioneering the application of latitude and longitude.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd22 9. **Division of the Circle into 360 Degrees**\nHe also introduced the division of a circle into 360 degrees into Greece.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udcbb 10. **Possible Inventor of the Antikythera Mechanism**\nHe is one of the strongest contenders for the honor of being the inventor of the Antikythera Mechanism (also known as the Antikythera Device), considered the world's first analogue computer.\n\n---\n\nIn summary, Hipparchus was a towering figure in the history of science, with lasting contributions to astronomy, mathematics, and geography.",
